            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AlyTibbz23"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I doubled the recipe and substituted the yellow mustard with spicy brown mustard and the ranch dressing dip with fiesta ranch dip for an extra kick! It tastes great!",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-24T21:02:34.527Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jtlangone"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were good but not great. They were a bit dry (possibly because of the ranch mix). Next time I will definately be using more Mayo. Also, way too much pepper. While I was grinding it out for the teaspoon measurement I thought it was a bit much, but wanted to follow the recipe to give a real review. I would say to use about half to 1/4 of the pepper. Also, what brings out the flavor in deviled eggs is salt, definately add a little. The ranch dressing gave it a little tang but took away from the mustard flavor that I love when having these. Good recipe for something different, but if you love traditional deviled eggs, you will probably only LIKE these.",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-05T18:30:47.027Z"
